  "solution": {
    "text": "In a perfectly inelastic collision between two particles, linear momentum is conserved. Let <math> <mrow> <mi>&#952;</mi> </mrow> </math>&nbsp;be the angle between the velocities of the two particles before the collision. Then<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>cos</mo><mi>&#952;</mi></math><br /><br />or&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>v</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>v</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>v</mi></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>v</mi></mrow></mfenced><mtext>cos</mtext><mi>&#952;</mi></math><br /><br />or&nbsp;<math> <mrow> <mn>1</mn> <mo>=</mo> <mn>1</mn> <mo>+</mo> <mn>1</mn> <mo>+</mo> <mn>2</mn> <mo>cos</mo> <mi>&#952;</mi> </mrow> </math><br /><br />or&nbsp;<math> <mrow> <mtext>cos</mtext> <mi>&#952;</mi> <mo>=</mo> <mo>-</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>1</mn> </mrow> <mrow> <mn>2</mn> </mrow> </mfrac> </mrow> </math><br /><br />or&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn><mn>0</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>",
